# 02 — Control Flow & Conditionals

## What is this?
Control flow statements allow your program to branch dynamically based on conditions using `if`, `else if`, `else`, and `switch`.

## What to Practice
Implement in `exercise.c`:
1. `int find_maximum(int a, int b, int c)`: Returns largest of three integers.
2. `char get_letter_grade(int score)`: Returns `'A'` (>=90), `'B'` (>=80), `'C'` (>=70), `'D'` (>=60), `'F'` (<60).
3. `int evaluate_operator(int a, int b, char op)`: Handles `'+'`, `'-'`, `'*'`, `'/'` (0 if `b==0`). Returns 0 for other operators.

## Reference Solution

