# 03 — Loops & Iteration

## What is this?
Loops execute code blocks repeatedly. C provides `for`, `while`, and `do-while`.

## What to Practice
Implement in `exercise.c`:
1. `int sum_range(int start, int end)`: Returns sum of integers from `start` to `end` inclusive (0 if `start > end`).
2. `long long factorial(int n)`: Returns `n!` (0 if `n < 0`, 1 if `n == 0`).
3. `int count_digits(int n)`: Returns digit count (handles negatives and 0).

## Reference Solution

<details>
<summary>Click to reveal reference solution</summary>

```c
int sum_range(int start, int end) {
    if (start > end) return 0;
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {
        sum += i;
    }
    return sum;
}

long long factorial(int n) {
    if (n < 0) return 0;
    long long res = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        res *= i;
    }
    return res;
}

int count_digits(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 1;
    if (n < 0) {
        if (n == -2147483648) return 10;
        n = -n;
    }
    int count = 0;
    while (n > 0) {
        count++;
        n /= 10;
    }
    return count;
}
```
