# 04 — Functions & Prototypes

## What is this?
Functions encapsulate reusable procedures. In C, prototypes inform the compiler of signatures before definition.

## What to Practice
Implement in `exercise.c`:
1. `int gcd(int a, int b)`: Greatest common divisor (returns positive int).
2. `int power(int base, int exp)`: `base^exp` (`exp >= 0`, `base^0 == 1`).
3. `int is_prime(int n)`: Returns 1 if prime, 0 otherwise (`<= 1` not prime).

## Reference Solution

<details>
<summary>Click to reveal reference solution</summary>

```c
int gcd(int a, int b) {
    if (a < 0) a = -a;
    if (b < 0) b = -b;
    while (b != 0) {
        int temp = b;
        b = a % b;
        a = temp;
    }
    return a;
}

int power(int base, int exp) {
    int result = 1;
    for (int i = 0; i < exp; i++) {
        result *= base;
    }
    return result;
}

int is_prime(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 0;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) return 0;
    }
    return 1;
}
```
