# 05 — Arrays & Pointer Basics

## What is this?
Arrays hold contiguous elements. Pointers store memory addresses. Array identifiers decay to pointers when passed to functions.

## What to Practice
Implement in `exercise.c`:
1. `void swap_integers(int *a, int *b)`: Swaps values pointed to by `a` and `b`.
2. `int array_sum(const int *arr, int length)`: Returns sum of array elements.
3. `int array_max(const int *arr, int length)`: Returns maximum element.

## Reference Solution

<details>
<summary>Click to reveal reference solution</summary>

```c
void swap_integers(int *a, int *b) {
    if (a == 0 || b == 0) return;
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}

int array_sum(const int *arr, int length) {
    if (arr == 0 || length <= 0) return 0;
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
        sum += arr[i];
    }
    return sum;
}

int array_max(const int *arr, int length) {
    if (arr == 0 || length <= 0) return 0;
    int max = arr[0];
    for (int i = 1; i < length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] > max) {
            max = arr[i];
        }
    }
    return max;
}
```
</details>

